# GitHub fine-grained PAT with "Contents: Read-only" on:
#   - Trophalaxeur/carbon-notes
#   - Trophalaxeur/gallium-homelab
#   - Trophalaxeur/neon-agents
# Required at build time to fetch blog articles, CV content, and aggregated docs.
# Without it, the loader logs a warning and skips the affected collections —
# the build still succeeds but those pages render empty.
# See docs/content-pipeline.md.
CONTENT_TOKEN=

# Optional. Absolute path to a local carbon-notes checkout. When set, CV content
# (cvSections, cvExperiences) is read from "$LOCAL_CARBON_NOTES/cv" via a local
# glob instead of the GitHub API — no token round-trip, instant reloads while
# editing CV content locally. Leave unset to always fetch from GitHub.
# LOCAL_CARBON_NOTES=/absolute/path/to/carbon-notes

# Optional. Port for the local preview server spun up by `npm run cv:pdf`.
# Defaults to 4322.
# PREVIEW_PORT=4322
